# Nuix Log Reviewer - classifier visibility defaults
#
# Controls whether entries carrying each classifier flag are shown or hidden by DEFAULT when logs
# are loaded. Hiding a classifier removes its entries from the current view (grid, counts, chart,
# patterns) by adding "AND NOT (flag:<name>)" to the running query.
#
# Format: one preference per line, as
#     <flag> = shown | hidden
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored. Any flag not listed here (or an unrecognized
# value) defaults to SHOWN. These are only DEFAULTS - you can flip any classifier's eye toggle in the
# Classifiers tab for the current session, and edit these defaults via Settings > Classifier Defaults.
#
# This file is read at startup / when the Classifier Defaults dialog saves. Example:
#     script = hidden
#     worker_state = hidden

# (No defaults set - all classifiers shown. Add "<flag> = hidden" lines or use the Settings dialog.)
